From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nak/sm50: Build integer multiplies from XMAD

IMUL and IMAD are slow variable-latency ops on Maxwell and Pascal.
Like the blob, build a 32-bit multiply-add from three full-rate 16x16
XMADs, a 16-bit one from a single XMAD, and the 32x32->64 product from
four XMADs and two PRMTs.  imad is formed for 32-bit values, and a 16-bit
iadd of an imul is folded into an imad.  XMADs take part in operand reuse
and bank-aware register allocation.

vkpeak on GM20B, in GIOPS: int32 1.8 -> 76, int16 1.8 -> 223,
int64 0.6 -> 17.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
